n\nThe tests were already committed in `8d9ea58` (`tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js`). Both acceptance commands pass: `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` ran 13 suites with 511 tests passing and 1 skipped, and `npx eslint tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js` is clean. The worktree is clean and I made no new changes or commits.\n\n**Entries for the Executor log (pinned by the tests, production code unchanged):**\n- **xlsx-only ZIP detection:** `getOfficeZipFormatBySignature` only recognises a ZIP as OOXML for xlsx. It looks for the xlsx markers in the last 8KB of the buffer. docx and pptx ZIPs are not identified this way, and markers outside that window are missed.\n- **TypeError on null:** `getOfficeZipFormatBySignature(null)` throws a TypeError instead of returning an \"unknown\" result.\n- **No `%PDF` detection:** `getDocumentFormatBySignature` does not recognise a PDF by its `%PDF` magic bytes, so a plain PDF buffer is not detected as PDF.\n- **pdfa written back as pdf:** the pdfa format is converted to the pdf format when it is written back, so the pdfa id does not round-trip.\n- **`getAllFormats('')` without a context throws:** calling it with an empty string and no operation context throws a TypeError.\n- **Stray `word` key:** the reviewer's rejection also mentioned a stray \"word\" key. I did not re-derive that one. It came from the review, and the log entry should be checked against the test file.\n\n**Decisions:** I asserted what the code does today and fixed nothing. I used small in-memory buffers with no binary fixtures.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- `formatchecker.js` signature detection is narrower than its name suggests: xlsx-only ZIP detection and no `%PDF` check.\n- `getAllFormats` and `getImageFormat` need an operation context. Use `operationContext.global` or a minimal fake.\n- A packet's target file list excludes the packet file, so executors cannot record their own log. The factory has to write it.","ttft_ms":2317,"type":"result","duration_ms":20981,"uui